<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian Wheat Board pool price cut A$10/t.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian Wheat Board pool price cut A$10/t.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Wheat Board (AWB) said on Monday it cut its pool price estimate for 1996/97 Australian Standard White (ASW) wheat by A$10.00 to A$195.00 a tonne fob.</p>
<p>Estimates for the higher protein Australian Hard and Prime Hard categories dropped by A$15.00 a tonne to A$210.00 and A$225.00 a tonne fob, respectively, the AWB said.</p>
<p>The next estimate is due on October 14, the AWB said.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
